{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-33986" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:{\\begin{aligned}x=4+3t \\\\ y=3+4t \\\\ z=-2+6t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:2x+5y+8z=229.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068245/state.json" "file_sha256" "a1074c1de2adf087665deb3c0bc0ff7a3a9db0fa2cde765b256b3e82dbeeb571"} {"question" "q-33986" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+5y+8z & =229 \\\\ 2(4+3t)+5(3+4t)+8(-2+6t) & =229 \\\\ 8+6t+15+20t-16+48t & =229 \\\\ 74t & =222 \\\\ t & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=3$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=4+3(3)=13 \\\\ y=3+4(3)=15 \\\\ z=-2+6(3)=16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $P(13,15,16).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068245/state.json" "file_sha256" "a1074c1de2adf087665deb3c0bc0ff7a3a9db0fa2cde765b256b3e82dbeeb571"} {"question" "q-33986" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068245/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "486d40b96c066a1f72548c248e866a2bf855d775e99dff51b0e149886b51b58b"} {"question" "q-33986" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068245/state.json" "file_sha256" "a1074c1de2adf087665deb3c0bc0ff7a3a9db0fa2cde765b256b3e82dbeeb571"} {"question" "q-33986" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-13,16,15)"] ["math" "(13,15,16)"] ["math" "(15,-13,16)"] ["math" "(2,5,8)"] ["text" "No intersection"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068245/state.json" "file_sha256" "a1074c1de2adf087665deb3c0bc0ff7a3a9db0fa2cde765b256b3e82dbeeb571"} {"question" "q-33986" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(13,15,16)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068245/state.json" "file_sha256" "a1074c1de2adf087665deb3c0bc0ff7a3a9db0fa2cde765b256b3e82dbeeb571"} {"question" "q-33987" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨3,5,9⟩+t⟨4,-1,6⟩,\\,Π:-2x+4y+2z-16=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068245/state.json" "file_sha256" "a1074c1de2adf087665deb3c0bc0ff7a3a9db0fa2cde765b256b3e82dbeeb571"} {"question" "q-33987" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's start by writing the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨3+4t,5-t,9+6t⟩.\n$$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x+4y+2z-16 & =0 \\\\ -2x+4y+2z & =16 \\\\ ⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,4,2⟩ & =16 \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-2,4,2⟩ & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨3+4t,5-t,9+6t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-2,4,2⟩ & =16 \\\\ ⟨3+4t,5-t,9+6t⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,4,2⟩ & =16 \\\\ -2(3+4t)+4(5-t)+2(9+6t) & =16 \\\\ -6-8t+20-4t+18+12t & =16 \\\\ 32 & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation has no solution. Therefore, we conclude that the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ do not intersect." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068245/state.json" "file_sha256" "a1074c1de2adf087665deb3c0bc0ff7a3a9db0fa2cde765b256b3e82dbeeb571"} {"question" "q-33987" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068245/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "486d40b96c066a1f72548c248e866a2bf855d775e99dff51b0e149886b51b58b"} {"question" "q-33987" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068245/state.json" "file_sha256" "a1074c1de2adf087665deb3c0bc0ff7a3a9db0fa2cde765b256b3e82dbeeb571"} {"question" "q-33987" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-2,4,2)"] ["math" "(3,5,9)"] ["math" "(4,-1,6)"] ["math" "(9,5,3)"] ["text" "No intersection"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068245/state.json" "file_sha256" "a1074c1de2adf087665deb3c0bc0ff7a3a9db0fa2cde765b256b3e82dbeeb571"} {"question" "q-33987" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "No intersection"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068245/state.json" "file_sha256" "a1074c1de2adf087665deb3c0bc0ff7a3a9db0fa2cde765b256b3e82dbeeb571"} {"question" "q-33992" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:{\\begin{aligned}x=5-2t \\\\ y=-1+4t \\\\ z=-3-5t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:2x-5y+3z-84=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068245/state.json" "file_sha256" "a1074c1de2adf087665deb3c0bc0ff7a3a9db0fa2cde765b256b3e82dbeeb571"} {"question" "q-33992" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-5y+3z-84 & =0 \\\\ 2(5-2t)-5(-1+4t)+3(-3-5t) & =84 \\\\ 10-4t+5-20t-9-15t & =84 \\\\ -39t & =78 \\\\ t & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=-2$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=5-2(-2)=9 \\\\ y=-1+4(-2)=-9 \\\\ z=-3-5(-2)=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is  $P(9,-9,7).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068245/state.json" "file_sha256" "a1074c1de2adf087665deb3c0bc0ff7a3a9db0fa2cde765b256b3e82dbeeb571"} {"question" "q-33992" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068245/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "486d40b96c066a1f72548c248e866a2bf855d775e99dff51b0e149886b51b58b"} {"question" "q-33992" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068245/state.json" "file_sha256" "a1074c1de2adf087665deb3c0bc0ff7a3a9db0fa2cde765b256b3e82dbeeb571"} {"question" "q-33992" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-9,9,7)"] ["math" "(5,-1,3)"] ["math" "(9,-9,7)"] ["math" "(9,7,-9)"] ["text" "No intersection"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068245/state.json" "file_sha256" "a1074c1de2adf087665deb3c0bc0ff7a3a9db0fa2cde765b256b3e82dbeeb571"} {"question" "q-33992" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(9,-9,7)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068245/state.json" "file_sha256" "a1074c1de2adf087665deb3c0bc0ff7a3a9db0fa2cde765b256b3e82dbeeb571"} {"question" "q-108368" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:{\\begin{aligned}x=4+2t \\\\ y=-3+4t \\\\ z=5t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:3x+2y-z=33.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068245/state.json" "file_sha256" "a1074c1de2adf087665deb3c0bc0ff7a3a9db0fa2cde765b256b3e82dbeeb571"} {"question" "q-108368" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+2y-z & =33 \\\\ 3(4+2t)+2(-3+4t)-(5t) & =33 \\\\ 12+6t-6+8t-5t & =33 \\\\ 9t & =27 \\\\ t & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=3$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=4+2(3)=10 \\\\ y=-3+4(3)=9 \\\\ z=5(3)=15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $P(10,9,15).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068245/state.json" "file_sha256" "a1074c1de2adf087665deb3c0bc0ff7a3a9db0fa2cde765b256b3e82dbeeb571"} {"question" "q-108368" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068245/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "486d40b96c066a1f72548c248e866a2bf855d775e99dff51b0e149886b51b58b"} {"question" "q-108368" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068245/state.json" "file_sha256" "a1074c1de2adf087665deb3c0bc0ff7a3a9db0fa2cde765b256b3e82dbeeb571"} {"question" "q-108368" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-6,-23,-25)"] ["math" "(10,9,15)"] ["math" "(2,-7,-5)"] ["math" "(20,29,40)"] ["text" "No intersection"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068245/state.json" "file_sha256" "a1074c1de2adf087665deb3c0bc0ff7a3a9db0fa2cde765b256b3e82dbeeb571"} {"question" "q-108368" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(10,9,15)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068245/state.json" "file_sha256" "a1074c1de2adf087665deb3c0bc0ff7a3a9db0fa2cde765b256b3e82dbeeb571"} {"question" "q-108891" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\frac{x+2}{3}=\\frac{y}{4}=\\frac{1-z}{2},\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨4,-3,1⟩=-9.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068245/state.json" "file_sha256" "a1074c1de2adf087665deb3c0bc0ff7a3a9db0fa2cde765b256b3e82dbeeb571"} {"question" "q-108891" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the equation of the line $l$, we know that it passes through the point $A(-2,0,1)$ and it is parallel to the vector $v=⟨3,4,-2⟩.$ Therefore, its vector equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =⟨-2,0,1⟩+t⟨3,4,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2+3t,4t,1-2t⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨-2+3t,4t,1-2t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨4,-3,1⟩ & =-9 \\\\ ⟨-2+3t,4t,1-2t⟩\\cdot ⟨4,-3,1⟩ & =-9 \\\\ 4(-2+3t)-3(4t)+(1-2t) & =-9 \\\\ -8+12t-12t+1-2t & =-9 \\\\ -2t & =-2 \\\\ t & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=1$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨-2+3(1),4(1),1-2(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,4,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get $P(1,4,-1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068245/state.json" "file_sha256" "a1074c1de2adf087665deb3c0bc0ff7a3a9db0fa2cde765b256b3e82dbeeb571"} {"question" "q-108891" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068245/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "486d40b96c066a1f72548c248e866a2bf855d775e99dff51b0e149886b51b58b"} {"question" "q-108891" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068245/state.json" "file_sha256" "a1074c1de2adf087665deb3c0bc0ff7a3a9db0fa2cde765b256b3e82dbeeb571"} {"question" "q-108891" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-2,0,1)"] ["math" "(1,4,-1)"] ["math" "(4,8,-3)"] ["math" "(5,4,-3)"] ["text" "No intersection"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068245/state.json" "file_sha256" "a1074c1de2adf087665deb3c0bc0ff7a3a9db0fa2cde765b256b3e82dbeeb571"} {"question" "q-108891" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(1,4,-1)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068245/state.json" "file_sha256" "a1074c1de2adf087665deb3c0bc0ff7a3a9db0fa2cde765b256b3e82dbeeb571"}] "usage" {"q-33992" [] "q-33986" []} "basis" 2285 "retractions" [[17592186120222 :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$l: {x = 4 + 3t; y = 3 + 4t; z =-2 + 6tandΠ: 2x + 5y + 8z = 229$."] [17592186120223 :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$l: {x = 5 - 2t; y =-1 + 4t; z =-3 - 5tandΠ: 2x - 5y + 3z - 84 = 0$."]] "immutable_answers" [17592186117833 17592186117834 17592186117835 17592186117836 17592186117837 17592186117839 17592186117840 17592186117841 17592186117842 17592186117843] "immutable_fields" [[17592186117832 :answer-field/correct] [17592186117832 :answer-field/id] [17592186117832 :answer-field/key] [17592186117832 :answer-field/type] [17592186117838 :answer-field/correct] [17592186117838 :answer-field/id] [17592186117838 :answer-field/key] [17592186117838 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
